# One account, in a config of its own rather than a fourth line in
# interop/baresip/config/accounts: docs/11-testing.md's "call, ended by the
# far end" needs baresip to hang up a call it just answered, and the only way
# this build of it can be made to (interop/baresip/config-hangup/config's own
# reasoning) is `ctrl_tcp` answering a command on a TCP port -- a module the
# shared container's config never loads, so the three phone-to-phone flows
# that peer already carries (interop/baresip/config/accounts) see no new
# account and no new port, whether or not this one's own flow ever runs.
#
# Same password as the other three (interop/kamailio/kamailio.cfg's own
# BARESIP_PASS): one more account sharing it costs this file nothing, and
# Kamailio already keys REGISTER and INVITE routing off the user part, not
# the password.
#
<sip:baresip-hangup@kamailio>;auth_pass=baresippass;answermode=auto;answerdelay=0;audio_codecs=pcmu,pcma;dtmfmode=rtpevent
